    <body>
        <segment id="1" parent="2" relname="circumstance">As I was scanning the ACM SIGCHI database</segment>
        <segment id="2" parent="26" relname="span">I found this article about the now famous or infamous Florida elections of 2000 and 2002.</segment>
        <segment id="3" parent="21" relname="span">Savage (2003), places the fault squarely on HCI professionals.</segment>
        <segment id="4" parent="23" relname="concession">He mentions that few reporters know what HCI is,</segment>
        <segment id="5" parent="23" relname="span">but he remains shocked that so many of the articles concerning the problem did not focus on the fact that these systems should be designed for regular people.</segment>
        <segment id="6" parent="5" relname="elaboration">In fact he points out that most people still expect new technology to be complicated to use.</segment>
        <segment id="7" parent="8" relname="antithesis">The article implies that the operators of the ballot boxes needed 12 hours of training in its use.</segment>
        <segment id="8" parent="24" relname="span">That is a bit off the 10-Minute mark set in our text.</segment>
        <segment id="9" parent="20" relname="span">Frankly, I did not think about this problem in this way until I read this article.</segment>
        <segment id="10" parent="9" relname="elaboration">I found myself blaming those individuals who could not properly learn to vote.</segment>
        <segment id="11" parent="25" relname="span">I find it hard to believe we could find a system that would have more potential for end-user collaborative design and implementation than the voting system.</segment>
        <segment id="12" parent="17" relname="circumstance">Given that NOVA is based in Florida,</segment>
        <segment id="13" parent="17" relname="span">does anyone in the class have a contact with the company building the replacement system?</segment>
        <segment id="14" parent="13" relname="evaluation">What an interesting opportunity to see if the HCI concepts are being used.</segment>
        <group id="15" type="span"/>
        <group id="16" type="span" parent="15" relname="span"/>
        <group id="17" type="span" parent="27" relname="span"/>
